Title:  The trips to London

Seq:    6.49.1.1

Level:  5 - Detail

Class:  quote

Attribution: [[Sandford, Christopher|Christopher Sandford]], 1999, from the book *[[Clapton : Edge of Darkness, Rev. Ed.]]*

Body:

The trips to London introduced him to a second tier of musicians — Junior Wells, J. B. Hutto, Hound Dog Taylor — for whose work [Dobell’s record store](https://theblackmusicrecordshop.co.uk/dobells/) was the sole British outlet. Clapton also possessed a reel-to-reel Grundig tape recorder with which, night after night, he honed his technique. According to Rose Clapp’s son Adrian, “\[Clapton\] swore and cursed till he could copy the sounds exactly, from as many records as he could get hold of.”

